      "refersTo": "pad-pass",
      "description": "Signature: nine square pads in fixed order, each with a drawn mark; failed names follow in rust.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-strip\"><div class=\"ds-pads\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Quality reading: 7 of 9 checks passed; failed: Sharpness, Glare.\"><span class=\"ds-pad\" data-state=\"pass\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"square\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5 6.5 11.5 12.5 4.5\"/></svg></span><span class=\"ds-pad\" data-state=\"pass\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"square\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5 6.5 11.5 12.5 4.5\"/></svg></span><span class=\"ds-pad\" data-state=\"pass\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"square\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5 6.5 11.5 12.5 4.5\"/></svg></span><span class=\"ds-pad\" data-state=\"pass\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"square\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5 6.5 11.5 12.5 4.5\"/></svg></span><span class=\"ds-pad\" data-state=\"fail\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"square\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 4 12 12M12 4 4 12\"/></svg></span><span class=\"ds-pad\" data-state=\"pass\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"square\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5 6.5 11.5 12.5 4.5\"/></svg></span><span class=\"ds-pad\" data-state=\"pass\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"square\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5 6.5 11.5 12.5 4.5\"/></svg></span><span class=\"ds-pad\" data-state=\"pass\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"square\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5 6.5 11.5 12.5 4.5\"/></svg></span><span class=\"ds-pad\" data-state=\"fail\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"square\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 4 12 12M12 4 4 12\"/></svg></span></div><span class=\"ds-strip-failed\">Sharpness, Glare</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-pad{display:inline-grid;place-items:center;width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:2px;color:var(--panel,#fdfefb)}.ds-pad[data-state=pass]{background:var(--pass,#1f7a4a)}.ds-pad[data-state=fail]{background:var(--reject,#ad3a17)}.ds-pad[data-state=none]{background:var(--pad-none,#dfe7d9);color:var(--muted-foreground,#4b4451);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--rule-strong,#7f8a79)}.ds-strip{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:4px 8px}.ds-pads{display:flex;gap:2px}.ds-strip-failed{font-family:var(--font-archivo,Archivo),system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:18px;color:var(--reject,#ad3a17)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "State Tag",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "pad-pass",
      "description": "Text state with a pad (Measured, Refused) or a line icon (Running in series blue). Never a pill.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-state ds-state-pass\"><span class=\"ds-pad\" data-state=\"pass\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"square\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 8.5 6.5 11.5 12.5 4.5\"/></svg></span>Measured</span> <span class=\"ds-state ds-state-fail\"><span class=\"ds-pad\" data-state=\"fail\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"square\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 4 12 12M12 4 4 12\"/></svg></span>Refused</span> <span class=\"ds-state ds-state-running\"><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M12 2v4M12 18v4M4.9 4.9l2.9 2.9M16.2 16.2l2.9 2.9M2 12h4M18 12h4M4.9 19.1l2.9-2.9M16.2 7.8l2.9-2.9\"/></svg>Running</span>",
      "css": ".ds-pad{display:inline-grid;place-items:center;width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:2px;color:var(--panel,#fdfefb)}.ds-pad[data-state=pass]{background:var(--pass,#1f7a4a)}.ds-pad[data-state=fail]{background:var(--reject,#ad3a17)}.ds-pad[data-state=none]{background:var(--pad-none,#dfe7d9);color:var(--muted-foreground,#4b4451);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--rule-strong,#7f8a79)}.ds-state{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;margin-right:16px;font-family:var(--font-archivo,Archivo),system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:500}.ds-state-pass{color:var(--pass,#1f7a4a)}.ds-state-fail{color:var(--reject,#ad3a17)}.ds-state-running{color:var(--series,#33578f)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Refusal Panel",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "refusal-panel",
      "description": "Rust-bordered wash panel naming each failed check and how to retake.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-refusal\" role=\"alert\"><h2>Why it was refused</h2><p>The photo failed the checks below, so it was not segmented and no value exists for it.</p><p class=\"ds-refusal-check\"><strong>Sharpness. The photo is out of focus or moved.</strong><br>Hold the camera still, tap to focus and retake.</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-refusal{padding:20px;background:var(--reject-wash,#f8e4dc);border:1px solid var(--reject,#ad3a17);border-radius:2px;font-family:var(--font-archivo,Archivo),system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--foreground,#1d1620)}.ds-refusal h2{margin:0;font-size:20px;line-height:26px;font-weight:700;font-stretch:78%}.ds-refusal p{margin:4px 0 0;font-size:14px;line-height:20px}.ds-refusal .ds-refusal-check{margin-top:16px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Warning Row",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "warning",
      "description": "Mustard-bordered caution row; icon in mustard ink.",
      "html": "<p class=\"ds-warn\"><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h17a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0zM12 9v4M12 17h.01\"/></svg>No scale was given, so values are in pixels.</p>",
      "css": ".ds-warn{display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:flex-start;margin:0;padding:8px 12px;background:var(--warn-wash,#fbf1cf);border:1px solid var(--warn,#d9a514);font-family:var(--font-archivo,Archivo),system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;color:var(--foreground,#1d1620)}.ds-warn svg{flex:none;margin-top:2px;color:var(--warn-ink,#664800)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Reagent Key",
    "overview": "The system is built like the colour key printed on a reagent bottle label. A dark aubergine shell holds pale reagent-green ground, white label panels sit on that ground, and every result is read against a row of square pads in fixed reading colours. Each colour means one thing. Green is pass, rust is a quality refusal, magenta is a system failure, amber is a caution, and blue is the one hue that carries no verdict at all.\n\nDensity is high and calm. A table row carries the strip, the value with its unit and basis, the date and the state without extra whitespace, and the columns stay where they are while only the values change. Hairline rules separate things, 2px corners keep everything square, and there is almost no shadow. Archivo, narrowed to 78% width, sets every heading. A tabular mono is used only for values. Motion is a hard step with no easing.\n\nThe build is light-only on purpose. It is neither a white-and-teal clinical dashboard nor a dark imaging viewer.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Aubergine shell (rail or header), reagent-green ground, white panels with hairline borders.",
      "Five verdict-bearing hues and one neutral series hue, never swapped.",
      "Square pads with a drawn mark (tick, cross, dash), so colour never stands alone.",
      "2px radius on every surface and control.",
      "Condensed Archivo headings, Spline Sans Mono only for values, IDs and dates.",
      "Pads step to their result in hard 90 ms frames. Nothing else moves."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Meaning Rule",
        "body": "Pass is green, a quality refusal is rust, and a system failure is magenta. The three are never interchangeable, and none of them ever decorates. If a colour does not state a verdict, it is a neutral or Series Blue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Verdict Hue Rule",
        "body": "Series Blue is the only colour for states and data that have no verdict yet or need none: the mask, Running, and the calibrated series. Do not use a verdict colour for an in-progress state, and do not use Series Blue for a result.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink-for-Text Rule",
        "body": "Mustard is a border and fill colour. Caution text and icons always use Mustard Ink.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Is Data Rule",
        "body": "Spline Sans Mono appears only on values, IDs and dates. It is never used for a heading, a label, a button or decoration. A metadata line is sans, with only the ID inside it in mono. When a value cell has no value (\"None\"), the word goes back to sans.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Condensed Heading Rule",
        "body": "Headings 1 to 3 are Archivo Bold at 78% width with balanced wrapping. Width carries the hierarchy, so headings never go uppercase or get letter-spacing.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Fixed Precision Rule",
        "body": "Values in a column show the same number of decimals (17.0 mm, never 17 mm). Physical values use one decimal, pixel values none. Negative values use a true minus sign. Dates read \"31 Oct 2026\".",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Label Rule",
        "body": "Panels, tables, pads and buttons have no shadow. If a surface does not float above the page, it has no shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Translucency Rule",
        "body": "The segmentation mask, in Series Blue at an opacity the user sets (55% by default), is the only translucent layer drawn over content. The modal scrim (aubergine at 70%) is the only other translucent layer, and it covers the page, not content.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do state every result with a pad mark or a word as well as its colour. Colour never stands alone.",
      "Do use Oxide Rust for a quality refusal, Reagent Magenta for a system failure and Pad Green for a pass, each with its own wash. Use Series Blue for the mask, Running and the calibrated series.",
      "Do keep every corner at 2px and every pad square.",
      "Do set values, units, IDs, hashes, versions and dates in Spline Sans Mono with tabular figures, at fixed precision per column.",
      "Do keep table columns at fixed widths. On narrow widths, stack rows into labelled blocks instead of letting the columns move.",
      "Do use Mustard Ink for caution text and keep Mustard for borders and fills.",
      "Do make hit targets at least 44px tall and use the global 2px Lifted Aubergine focus outline.",
      "Do mark any stand-in image as constructed, in both its accessible name and its visible label."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use Pad Green, Oxide Rust or Reagent Magenta as interchangeable \"error\" or \"accent\" colours, or as decoration.",
      "Don't show a Running or pending state in a verdict colour.",
      "Don't set Mustard text on a light ground.",
      "Don't use mono for headings, labels, buttons or ornament.",
      "Don't add shadows to panels, pads or buttons. The menu shadow is for floating layers only.",
      "Don't ease or tween result motion. Pads snap in hard steps.",
      "Don't round pads or turn state tags into pills.",
      "Don't add a translucent layer over content other than the segmentation mask."
    ]
  }
}